From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] inetcomm: IMimeBody property set operations, EnumProps, display name, IsType, CopyTo (2046)

inetcomm: IMimeBody property set operations, EnumProps, display name, IsType, CopyTo.

SetPropInfo keeps the charset, flags, row number and encoding of a property
(GetPropInfo reports them and the number of values), AppendProp adds another
instance of a property, CopyProps, MoveProps and DeleteExcept work on named
properties (all of them for a NULL list), QueryProp matches a value, Clone
copies the properties, EnumProps returns an IMimeEnumProperties (Next, Skip,
Reset, Clone, Count; EPF_NONAME), Set/GetDisplayName follow the file name,
IsType answers IBT_ATTACHMENT, IBT_SECURE and IBT_CSETTAGGED (a message's
first text part is not an attachment, the others are) and CopyTo copies the
properties and the data to another body. They were stubs.
